obs the standing-equipment.kyri roster uses `guard <name>` for the short handle and a separate `path tools/gen/chapter/<name>_witness.rish` line for the actual file -- the two need not share a prefix, which is why a naive basename-to-guard-name comparison overcounts unrostered witnesses; the correct measure reads the `path` field
obs the writer-sheds bound is arithmetic rather than tidiness: 1,175 bytes of headroom against accounts running 2,000-3,900 means the card overflows by construction on the very next honest account, which is exactly what happened here
